It's amazing to see such models fully trained on synthetic data. Looking forward to playing with them.

@AmelieTabatta highlights the release of GLiNER2.5, the most significant update to the GLiNER architecture. This version introduces a boundary prediction architecture that predicts entity start and end points, removing limits on entity length and enabling inference on full documents.

GLiNER2.5 offers five new capabilities: long-context extraction and classification, unlimited span lengths, joint information extraction, constrained classification, and span attributes. A series of demo videos will showcase these features on real data during GLiNER2.5 Week. The model's architecture, benchmarks, and use cases are detailed in the launch blog by Fastino Labs.
